    "summary": "For much of the financial services industry, the conversation around AI has focused on creating efficiencies by automating processes, reducing costs, and replacing manual work. But banks may be overlooking AI’s biggest opportunity. Rather than focusing on what AI can eliminate, financial institutions may find greater value in using the technology to better understand their Read more...\nThe post Why Spade’s Oban MacTavish Thinks Banking AI Should Focus on Revenue, Not Cost Cutting appeared first on Finovate.",
    "hasSummary": true,
